st's) are read by `seon.fx/read-source` on an effect worker and written on the boot's `:seon.root/source` fact (`seon.root/import-source!`) only when the running binary is built from that tree (`target/seon.tree`, `seon.fx/tree-id`), else `:unshared` says why; an agent uses only its root's current boot's inputs and keeps its greens in the shared results directory (:seon.config.source/test-results-dir) through root's :file owner: the owner ruled (2026-10-23) that a test that is the same is not run again once green, \"especially when freshly branched\", so an agent's greens and a checkout's are one store (seon.agent-test/an-agents-greens-and-a-checkouts-are-one-store). A shard compares the planned tree before storing, so an edit during a run never stores a green under the unedited digests. v1 keyed a result by its reach digest (~/src/seon seon.test.cache). Open: shards are balanced by test count, not time; seon.source-test/a-restart-catches-up-and-a-new-generation-resumes waits on an `nc -w 600` that never times out an idle connection on macOS."
