  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.proofs/prove-runs-what-a-change-reaches"}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-test-runs-the-binary-through-binary-sh"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-23 (shrink session): seon.config-test/bin-ports-writes-its-keys-under-their-current-names runs bin/ports, which runs ./seon ports, through clojure.java.shell/sh directly, not through seon.test-store/binary-sh, the one call seon.program/graph-index's :binary? counts (:seon.config.source/binary-vars). So bin/test's plan does not build target/seon for it, and on a worktree whose binary is another tree's it is red for a reason that is not the change (config refused: unknown keys). Correct: every test that runs the binary or a script that runs it (bin/root, bin/check, bin/ports, bin/mcp, ./seon) does so through binary-sh, and a law over test/'s forms (read as data) is red on a shell call naming one of them another way, as seon.check-test/every-test-root-starts-through-start-root! is for roots."
